<%= UiComponents::Lookbook::TableOfContents.call(page) %>

An "on this page" sidebar that highlights the links whose headings are in view.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/toc)

<%= embed AppicaUI::TocPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
Toc(aria_label: "On this page", root_margin: "-64px 0px 0px 0px") do
  TocList do
    @article.headings.each do |heading|
      TocItem { TocLink(href: "##{heading.anchor}", depth: heading.level) { heading.text } }
    end
  end
end
```

Each `TocLink` points at a heading's `id`. The `appica-ui--toc` controller observes those headings and marks the links
whose heading is in view `data-active`; the topmost one also gets `aria-current="location"`, and the indicator on the
rail slides over them. With nothing in view the heading nearest the top wins. Give headings `scroll-mt-*` so they
aren't hidden under a sticky header when a link jumps to them, and offset the tracking boundary with `root_margin:`.

The examples track a scrolling panel with `container:`, which also makes clicks scroll that panel; on a normal page
leave it out and the anchors jump the page.

