## API reference

### Toc

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `aria_label:` | `String` | "Table of contents" | The landmark's name (translated). |
| `root_margin:` | `String` | `"0px"` | IntersectionObserver margin - offset the boundary for a sticky header. |
| `container:` | `String` | - | A CSS selector of the scrolling element to track (and scroll on click). |

### TocLink

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|------|------|---------|-------------|
| `href:` | `String` | - | **Required.** `#id` of the heading. |
| `depth:` | `Integer` | `2` | The heading level (2-6), indenting deeper entries. |

A block that takes an argument receives the attributes for your own element. `TocList` is the `<ul>` with the rail,
`TocItem` an `<li>`.

## Accessibility

- A `<nav>` landmark named "Table of contents" - rename it ("On this page") to suit the page.
- The topmost link in view is `aria-current="location"`; the scroll-spy never moves focus or scrolls by itself.
- Links are ordinary anchors; the indicator and link transitions honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.
